# Tailwind Values

This project uses Tailwind v4, where spacing, sizing, z-index, scale, and
similar utilities accept any integer. Do not reach for `[...]` arbitrary
values when a numeric utility expresses the same thing.

- Spacing scale is `0.25rem` per unit: `52rem` is `w-208`, `14rem` is `w-56`,
  `18rem` is `w-72`.
- Applies to `w-*`, `h-*`, `size-*`, `min-*`/`max-*`, `p-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`,
  `inset-*`/`top-*`/`left-*`, `translate-*`, `z-*`, `scale-*`, `duration-*`.

```html
<!-- Bad -->
<div class="w-[52rem] z-[1] group-hover:scale-[1.15]" />

<!-- Good -->
<div class="w-208 z-1 group-hover:scale-115" />
```

Brackets are fine only when there is no utility equivalent: `calc()`, `min()`,
`clamp()`, viewport units like `60svh`, unitless `leading-[1.08]`, and font
sizes outside the type scale.
